<section class="section has-text-centered">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="has-text-weight-bold is-size-1 is-size-3-mobile is-uppercase">Amex F1</p>
    <p class="projectdescription is-size-5">
      For Amex’s first year driving into the world of F1, we set out to create experiences that resonated with both longtime fans and those just discovering the sport. From Mexico City to Japan to Las Vegas, Wasserman and the IAT ensured Amex showed up not just as a sponsor, but as a brand delivering service, access, and entertainment – all core to their DNA. Across the season, we brought to life multi-story Fan Experiences, private suites, and immersive brand moments. We launched their partnership with F1 Academy, debuting a custom driver suit and car livery, further cementing Amex’s commitment to the sport’s future. Alongside this, we built an AI-powered hype-trailer generator, viewing decks with unmatched perspectives of the track, our own “infinity room” reimagining a mirrored garage, customizable livery patches and fan giveaways, and more – establishing Amex as a major player in F1’s newest markets.    </p>
    <br>
    <p class="has-text-weight-bold is-size-4">Collaborators:</p>
    <p class="collabnames is-family-secondary has-text-weight-bold is-size-4 is-italic"> Jason Fischer // Ward Williams // Eunhae Kang // Sean Cowie <br> Zuzu Boisson // Caleb VanDyke // Bri Garza</p>
  </div>
</section>

